      "message": "Not blocking: this checkout\u0027s cleanup step is the one step after Muse that can still get an OIDC token. It is safe only while Muse\u0027s sandbox can\u0027t write `.git`.\n\n`actions/checkout` runs a cleanup at the end of the job. It runs with the job\u0027s environment, which includes `ACTIONS_ID_TOKEN_REQUEST_*`, because the step-level blanking doesn\u0027t reach it. The cleanup runs `git submodule foreach --recursive ...` in the workspace, and that reads the index, which runs `core.fsmonitor`. I checked with a repository whose `.git/config` sets `core.fsmonitor` to a script that touches a file. `git config --get-regexp` didn\u0027t run it, but checkout\u0027s `submodule foreach` line did. So the comment\u0027s \"every later step has no way to ask for an OIDC token\" holds only while `.git` stays read-only in the sandbox. The skill says it is in CI, which is why this isn\u0027t blocking.\n\nFix: check out main with plain `git` in a `run` step, as `changes` and `verify` do (`git init`, `git fetch --depth\u003d1`, `git checkout`), so no action\u0027s cleanup runs after Muse. Alternatively, say in the comment that the boundary depends on the sandbox keeping `.git` read-only.",
